// apps/hub/deck.jsonc — the hub defines the hub.
//
// Per-app serve config (the `AppServeConfig` shape deck consumes). Loaded by
// shipd via the app-registration port; deck-config owns the schema + parser.
//
// Post deck-jsonc-simplify cutover, the file only carries the
// non-conventional bits. `name`/`route`/`source`/`render` moved to
// host-owned binds (apps.jsonc + convention):
//
//   - name   → derived from the directory basename (`apps/hub` ⇒ `hub`)
//   - route  → declared in apps.jsonc (`apps/shipd/apps.jsonc`)
//   - source → always `<root>/.deck` (the bundler's out_dir)
//   - render → defaults to csr (the implicit posture every app served in)
//
// Framework clients (`@ship/sdk-client` etc.) are NO LONGER host-declared
// here — they are provider-declared in their own `package.json#deckFramework`
// and discovered by walking the app's resolved dependency graph (see
// `/home/madvib/dev/sui//home/madvib/dev/sui/crates/deck/deck-bundler/src/app.rs::discover_deck_frameworks`). The
// framework never hardcodes any ship path; every singleton owner names
// itself.
//
// What the file CAN carry (the only non-conventional pieces):
//
//   entry? { clientsModule, exposeNames }   host-owned entry bootstrap
//                                            the bundler emits as
//                                            `entry.gen.ts`: imports the
//                                            data tables from
//                                            `routes.gen`, constructs
//                                            the named `clients` map off
//                                            `clientsModule`'s exports,
//                                            and calls `mountRouter`.
//                                            `exposeNames` becomes the
//                                            keys the runtime exposes to
//                                            every view's
//                                            `ctx.clients.<name>`.
{
  "entry": {
    "clientsModule": "./src/lib/client.ts",
    "exposeNames": ["ship", "ops"]
  }
}
